#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124249 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "289ae874-f555-50ee-896f-eb2188004124" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Eigenvalues of a 3x3 Matrix Containing a Block of Zeros"}] :question/id #uuid "4b2fcf5d-0da3-5676-b4c6-54095c3fb45c" :question/math-academy-id "e-5486" :question/problem "Determine all real eigenvalues $\\lambda$ of the matrix \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/assets/9c2a25dabbe750ebb52b4de6dbee954df55c09a8ceaf0b82eef346b5a337c544.png)" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\, A-\\lambda I \\mathbin{:}$\n﻿﻿﻿![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/assets/947389b453c22e1b56704ec6a1cdf8e7e529ea9a944c57d3e55a471ab3539569.png)\n\nThe characteristic equation is $\\det(A-\\lambda I) = 0.$ \n\nSince the determinant of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix is given by the product of the entries on the main diagonal, we obtain the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-9-\\lambda  & 4 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 9-\\lambda  & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-9-\\lambda )(9-\\lambda )(6-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +9)(\\lambda -9)(\\lambda -6) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda_1=-9,$ $\\lambda_2=9,$ and $\\lambda_3=6.$ \n\n**Note:** The eigenvalues of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix are always the entries on the main diagonal."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124250 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5abea3ab-76a7-5598-8ede-b4cf88dd47d7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Eigenvalues of a General 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "76c52a74-9b98-5df5-ac63-64e92af1a580" :question/math-academy-id "e-5487" :question/problem "Determine all real eigenvalues ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/assets/dc652e29fc17e565962d96a947980358f776d5e37816269dbe9139328889fc3f.png) of the matrix \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/assets/a93a99c9a1491b842d5b8d30c90f37b06528d0bd1b82bb5257d84ecb43a2b288.png)" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/assets/0d5fcfb7528ad4e3fcf0e7f173d9bd0be80d5148b6c1bda8a9bb765dc772d1e2.png)\n﻿﻿﻿![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/assets/619fe52f77e282e97915de285e8384d784dc6352eb06295e6991a1bdb2bae1c3.png)\n\nThe characteristic equation is given by ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/assets/02f21e39c78b5ad8b88c5040d074fe78a5e6950760f2653b724c4e27627752ba.png) \n\nExpanding the determinant across the ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/assets/ac192f9c9318b0668e9dee7e695d4dd383f2d74df0298ef6dd4861d421e97afb.png)st row, we get the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/assets/7062cb3cf1cf9e2dc2cac6c69537dd6c20c5b211f641a511092d7fbf8457d9de.png)\n\nNow, we need to solve this equation. We find the first root by testing some values. According to the rational zeros theorem, a list of good first guesses consists of all divisors of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/assets/97622f2aa4af27b2ce48c21c48e49129b58197dd2d02a3dddb5ff3685ba8197e.png) \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/assets/a40f8317b6de6727323c39a9e8105822544f88727eb855ce5e89c71cc185c485.png)\n\nLet's pick ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/assets/4b7d6cca59677b4ec63fc9997d5d32c4d2e67f87d45b89540e42293f4ed1ba73.png) Substituting to the characteristic equation gives\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/assets/146529d47426ad676072aeba20837a6da7ea5dc400a17f37dd3cb4d0a5c7f107.png)\nSo, ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/assets/f161fa211fd6dda217ad08855ed96703b8f620aeb1485d67562f3bf1666928d7.png) is a root of the equation. This means we can factor ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/assets/210f39779d00613e2fcc094145f31e789ae93a0361618ae6b4623c107272799f.png) out of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/assets/b8b832cc07ffad66665f2b961a9d78d97a0a89caac7ffc765e065a6d0946d0f6.png) using synthetic division:\n\n| ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/assets/124a84b4788cb014c01f416a1e0433eb7991fd3c4c792400892377f4f3407221.png) | ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/assets/e12ac0c95825bef841bc95fa94b20bf787e03ec405c223a26fab4a73c61efa10.png) | ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/assets/783e116511a2ce8a0ad54bedf9e79e7b8d380fc31dae50f43d1c4ce51a305354.png) | ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/assets/cc8c6a49685acb757524d62a8cbb6805c5198485f888874bbbb66968aa9e6178.png) | ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/assets/aeffa7b19c9d0bea2c544ec3cc1aa53ad8b44271b89f115e7a4db58ecfd33720.png) |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/assets/c84a10b5fd2ed823a1f173f8120dd2250031ad7e5f10424ef0d3cd91ec148bed.png) | ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/assets/2f84eb7bb5c17949d98cacb1f217bbbd99ef39032a3a0a960412d0e94bcba8b6.png) | ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/assets/df9b41873d2d60b97b90650e0713641a8647a38205427f8f8fe04cef9237646b.png) | ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/assets/ee595b41249fe71b2b1dbc2d31b9eb9069bd31e887f4bf62456ab05dd926318e.png) |\n|  | ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/assets/1baad26e6ade455fffeb4304606352ecfbf86e67e4cb47c35b736f59e44d009b.png) | ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/assets/af11b6c6dc78667e7d9c0d4acfeccea8ce8e6f83f49e3213083c8bff30c4fd14.png) | ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/assets/30accb457d578da8be84827af0d559e9f57f0d18d08f8df490dc88879f8c90e7.png) | ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/assets/278088cea7543d913bd6e9702b03c58ff40e05413a543120087373c426bad83e.png) |\n\nSo, we obtain the following factorization:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/assets/b7457336851f79803231c1d2d64a07591ff7bb5e1f3315dd8af98bfe2782bcb4.png)\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/assets/6528f51e5d19fcda74b8ca490c4fd89b3e43269b57053da77b29284702c1f833.png) ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/assets/8c25f2182438cde814f01fd81ad6e94684ceed686db04002e7934b310e3261b1.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/assets/5e20e499636e1ce842b9d25a9934ce6956334c31f56d9cfd22f5230fbcbce983.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124298 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef311af0-0e95-5574-a151-2971ad66bd08" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Eigenvalues of a 4x4 Matrix Containing a Block of Zeros"}] :question/id #uuid "a1c51187-c0a6-505c-bc58-2319b439086e" :question/math-academy-id "e-7047" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/assets/2379f9f0cec3f257da5a4c0695f114d0bc7f3b4c914edabfd690ff94705faceb.png)\n\nConsider the matrix $P$ given above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $\\lambda=4$ is an eigenvalue of $P$\n\n- $\\lambda=-1$ is an eigenvalue of $P$\n\n- The eigenvalue $\\lambda=6$ has algebraic multiplicity $2$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\, P-\\lambda I \\mathbin{:}$\n﻿﻿﻿![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/assets/8ee9ef991440e5641d6a458c0384382b54eb3d8504856b942fc33cf24b0b85e9.png)\n\nThe characteristic equation is $\\det(P-\\lambda I) = 0.$ \n\nNotice that we can expand the $4 \\times 4$ determinant across the $1$st column, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & 0 & -8 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1-\\lambda  & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -3 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 4-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 7 & -3 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, expanding the $3 \\times 3$ determinant across the $2$nd row, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3-\\lambda )\\cdot (4-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & 5 \\\\ 7 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )(4-\\lambda )((-1-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda )-35) & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )(4-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-36) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -3)(\\lambda -4)(\\lambda -6)(\\lambda +6) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the eigenvalues of $P$ are $\\lambda=3,$ $\\lambda=4,$ $\\lambda=6,$ and $\\lambda=-6$ (all with algebraic multiplicity $1$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360392 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "289ae874-f555-50ee-896f-eb2188004124" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Eigenvalues of a 3x3 Matrix Containing a Block of Zeros"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e44d3298-65f4-56a6-9eb7-0c0057ca0ae8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in {3,0,6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360394} {:answer/id #uuid "0714fec2-c0cf-5990-90c2-c21f57dbedb0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in {3,4,9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360395} {:answer/id #uuid "2d0e4b7b-ca76-5bda-a6b2-38485033e3a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in {3,-2,6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360396} {:answer/id #uuid "b25d4d6b-7fa7-5d7e-bd3f-4b7e5ed63218" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in {3,4,6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360397} {:answer/id #uuid "bfc8089c-9cb3-55cf-af77-8a3c85e18ff3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in {-3,4,6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360398}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b25d4d6b-7fa7-5d7e-bd3f-4b7e5ed63218" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in {3,4,6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360397} :answer-field/id #uuid "13700d7b-91ba-5b16-9317-ecb5fb5190fe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360393}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f772a19b-8ab2-5f26-9ef1-47231e01914d" :question/math-academy-id "q-140449" :question/problem "Determine all real eigenvalues $\\lambda $ of the matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 6\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}4-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 3-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 6-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(A-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nSince the determinant of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix is given by the product of the entries on the main diagonal, we obtain the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}4-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 3-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 6-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )(3-\\lambda )(6-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -4)(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda -6) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are ${\\lambda }_{1}=3,$ $\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=4,$ and ${\\lambda }_{3}=6.$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvalues of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix are always the entries on the main diagonal."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360399 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef311af0-0e95-5574-a151-2971ad66bd08" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Eigenvalues of a 4x4 Matrix Containing a Block of Zeros"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a0fded2-ac9c-5437-9236-65c121f82c76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360401} {:answer/id #uuid "a5d1578d-4cb5-5420-ae87-122043255126" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360402} {:answer/id #uuid "6b33ede0-1ce7-56a0-a5df-0c8c7ab20259" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360403} {:answer/id #uuid "c79cd94f-34d2-56ce-894e-6e609c3549c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360404} {:answer/id #uuid "3cb1039a-08f6-5305-80e0-d0a938815b73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360405}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c79cd94f-34d2-56ce-894e-6e609c3549c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360404} :answer-field/id #uuid "492b4a75-3451-5d04-92fd-2f0fe38420f6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360400}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9ecc9ad3-e2ba-5fb3-b1f1-c3971775671e" :question/math-academy-id "q-140450" :question/problem "$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & -6 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -4 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $P$ given above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $\\lambda =0$ is an eigenvalue of $P$\n- $\\lambda =-4$ is an eigenvalue of $P$\n- The eigenvalue $\\lambda =2$ has algebraic multiplicity $2$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,P-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nP-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}5-\\lambda  & 2 & -6 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -\\lambda  & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -4-\\lambda  & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(P-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nNotice that we can expand the $4\\times 4$ determinant across the $1$st column, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}5-\\lambda  & 2 & -6 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -\\lambda  & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -4-\\lambda  & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (5-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}-\\lambda  & 0 & 7 \\\\ -3 & -4-\\lambda  & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, expanding the $3\\times 3$ determinant across the $3$rd row, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(5-\\lambda )\\cdot (2-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ -3 & -4-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (5-\\lambda )(2-\\lambda )(-\\lambda )(-4-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -5)(\\lambda -2)\\lambda (\\lambda +4) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the eigenvalues of $P$ are $\\lambda =5,$ $\\lambda =2,$ $\\lambda =0,$ and $\\lambda =-4$  (all with algebraic multiplicity $1$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360406 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef311af0-0e95-5574-a151-2971ad66bd08" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Eigenvalues of a 4x4 Matrix Containing a Block of Zeros"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cefb8419-40ce-5cc3-a557-5f463855cc8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -1)(\\lambda +4)(\\lambda -8)(\\lambda +5)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360408} {:answer/id #uuid "903adb35-9bfa-510e-90bf-ea53b460b4e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -7)(\\lambda +4)(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda +5)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360409} {:answer/id #uuid "5f357b7a-a968-5ef8-b69c-a98b188ccc1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda +7)(\\lambda +4)(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda -2)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360410} {:answer/id #uuid "8d3ad5f3-c593-5589-b3fa-5454d895a1c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -7)(\\lambda +4)(\\lambda +5)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360411} {:answer/id #uuid "445ebe4c-5a57-5934-b05d-cb31e30e72b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -7)(\\lambda +4)(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda -5)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360412}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "903adb35-9bfa-510e-90bf-ea53b460b4e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -7)(\\lambda +4)(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda +5)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360409} :answer-field/id #uuid "d17c83f0-6240-52e2-b8dc-6604507cf6cb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360407}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c7cd0c11-0503-560e-b7d4-459fb0540332" :question/math-academy-id "q-140471" :question/problem "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n$P=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 6 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -5\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,P-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nP-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}7-\\lambda  & 6 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4-\\lambda  & 0 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3-\\lambda  & 11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(P-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nSince the determinant of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix is given by the product of the entries on the main diagonal, we obtain the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}7-\\lambda  & 6 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4-\\lambda  & 0 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3-\\lambda  & 11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (7-\\lambda )(-4-\\lambda )(3-\\lambda )(-5-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -7)(\\lambda +4)(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda +5) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360413 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5abea3ab-76a7-5598-8ede-b4cf88dd47d7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Eigenvalues of a General 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b3f02453-061b-56f3-bfa0-a2ffbe3778ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}+2{\\lambda }^{2}-13\\lambda +10=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360415} {:answer/id #uuid "798ac345-1a15-5080-8724-fe75d9fb6a75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}+13{\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda +4=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360416} {:answer/id #uuid "d8a3e926-e46e-5b32-8178-fddfad35b0cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}-2{\\lambda }^{2}-13\\lambda +25=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360417} {:answer/id #uuid "567fb19b-9406-5b40-849b-28b42ca090d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}-2{\\lambda }^{2}-13\\lambda -30=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360418} {:answer/id #uuid "7f2b09b9-4f5c-5972-8f6f-3d39d5f12e11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}+2{\\lambda }^{2}+13\\lambda -15=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360419}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b3f02453-061b-56f3-bfa0-a2ffbe3778ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}+2{\\lambda }^{2}-13\\lambda +10=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360415} :answer-field/id #uuid "04e97fc9-c02b-54b1-b844-e543dff3515e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360414}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e1fed639-500d-5637-9314-77381d4239bd" :question/math-academy-id "q-140515" :question/problem "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n$C=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,C-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nC-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & -1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(C-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nExpanding the determinant across the $1$st row, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(C-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & -1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}-3-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ 2 & -2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}|-(-1)|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}|+(-1)|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3-\\lambda  \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}+5\\lambda )+(-\\lambda -5)-(5+\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (-{\\lambda }^{3}-2{\\lambda }^{2}+15\\lambda )-\\lambda -5-5-\\lambda  & =0 \\\\ -{\\lambda }^{3}-2{\\lambda }^{2}+13\\lambda -10 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{3}+2{\\lambda }^{2}-13\\lambda +10 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360420 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef311af0-0e95-5574-a151-2971ad66bd08" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Eigenvalues of a 4x4 Matrix Containing a Block of Zeros"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a55e2efa-8a04-5f25-8922-92ec59bbbaf3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -6)^{2}(\\lambda +7)(\\lambda +2)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360422} {:answer/id #uuid "7dfa30de-bbee-53c1-9abe-937ef3ea82de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -6)(\\lambda +6)(\\lambda +7)(\\lambda +2)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360423} {:answer/id #uuid "3585b816-a104-5c3c-86b2-7faeaa866408" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -6)(\\lambda +7)(\\lambda +2)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360424} {:answer/id #uuid "ec022287-4ec7-5d5e-9a88-4f2911268b83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -6)(\\lambda +6)(\\lambda -7)(\\lambda -2)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360425} {:answer/id #uuid "7c46d776-ca14-5e9a-a854-4a0be2cf06ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -6)^{2}(\\lambda -7)(\\lambda -2)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360426}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a55e2efa-8a04-5f25-8922-92ec59bbbaf3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -6)^{2}(\\lambda +7)(\\lambda +2)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360422} :answer-field/id #uuid "572d8d26-c351-5a69-bb59-ea1f519173de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360421}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d240320f-4168-5ae1-a3dc-306aaeeb5354" :question/math-academy-id "q-36843" :question/problem "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}6-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -7-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(A-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nSince the determinant of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix is given by the product of the entries on the main diagonal, we obtain the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}6-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -7-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (6-\\lambda )(-7-\\lambda )(6-\\lambda )(-2-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -6)^{2}(\\lambda +7)(\\lambda +2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124933 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "289ae874-f555-50ee-896f-eb2188004124" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Eigenvalues of a 3x3 Matrix Containing a Block of Zeros"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fa0ef8ff-9fec-507b-862c-a9f0e17b6225" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1 - λ)(λ^{2} + λ - 16) = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122621} {:answer/id #uuid "0394eed9-f552-5dad-a903-5c47d8323de5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1 - λ)(λ^{2} + λ + 4) = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122622} {:answer/id #uuid "19ff8716-e2a6-5629-80f6-c6807a9f8e99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1 - λ)(λ^{2} + λ - 4) = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122623} {:answer/id #uuid "4c044c6d-cef5-5628-b2d4-aeb11b1848ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1 - λ)(λ^{2} + λ - 10) = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122624} {:answer/id #uuid "6c2f700f-2d6f-5fe4-98de-ef176065458c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1 - λ)(λ^{2} - 16) = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122625}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa0ef8ff-9fec-507b-862c-a9f0e17b6225" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1 - λ)(λ^{2} + λ - 16) = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122621} :answer-field/id #uuid "513cd4e0-dd21-5dc0-8816-a326879209bb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122620}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2accab64-f6f1-5300-b0aa-a3471aee3ef9" :question/math-academy-id "q-36845" :question/problem "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}-3-\\lambda  & 2 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 2-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(A-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nExpanding the determinant across the $3$rd row, we obtain the following:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-3-\\lambda  & 2 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 2-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}-3-\\lambda  & 2 \\\\ 5 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )((-3-\\lambda )(2-\\lambda )-2\\cdot 5) & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda -16) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360427 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "289ae874-f555-50ee-896f-eb2188004124" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Eigenvalues of a 3x3 Matrix Containing a Block of Zeros"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a3e7f30c-f81a-57b0-acc2-3d20f5428f78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda (\\lambda -2)(\\lambda +2)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360429} {:answer/id #uuid "fd72688e-9a02-53f0-97b4-a015ad6f91cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -1)(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda -2)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360430} {:answer/id #uuid "b7961078-4bc8-53ca-b41f-57f2d9c4c8be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -1)(\\lambda +3)(\\lambda -2)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360431} {:answer/id #uuid "27d171fb-2b6d-513f-8e7d-3aced11830c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda +1)(\\lambda -1)(\\lambda +1)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360432} {:answer/id #uuid "e2042c0b-850e-5f19-8300-eb6487bcf00e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda +1)(\\lambda +3)(\\lambda -2)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360433}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e2042c0b-850e-5f19-8300-eb6487bcf00e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda +1)(\\lambda +3)(\\lambda -2)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360433} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c9d897a-ac21-54d0-a991-410c149ebcd0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360428}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "575aa320-c74e-5266-82e6-e8a0338048e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-36860" :question/problem "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}-2-\\lambda  & 0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1-\\lambda  & -1 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(A-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nExpanding the determinant across the $2$nd column, we obtain the following:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-2-\\lambda  & 0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1-\\lambda  & -1 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-1-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}-2-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-1-\\lambda )((-2-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda )-(-2)(-2)) & =0 \\\\ (-1-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda -6) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +1)(\\lambda +3)(\\lambda -2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360434 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "289ae874-f555-50ee-896f-eb2188004124" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Eigenvalues of a 3x3 Matrix Containing a Block of Zeros"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a242941f-f2f7-50ba-9bab-fd846d68afc8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda +2)({\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda +10)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360436} {:answer/id #uuid "161311e1-e355-556c-978e-16b024e293d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -2)({\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda +10)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360437} {:answer/id #uuid "b97a0964-53f2-5c3c-aa92-3fd44114c849" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda +2)({\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda -10)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360438} {:answer/id #uuid "da51c6ac-1022-5800-9c2f-052f43258537" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -1)^{2}(\\lambda +2)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360439} {:answer/id #uuid "bcc42793-33f7-534b-883c-f3243664ac50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda +3)(\\lambda +2)(\\lambda -3)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360440}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a242941f-f2f7-50ba-9bab-fd846d68afc8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda +2)({\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda +10)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360436} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d69bddc-0fd1-5b2b-a519-1f3571f9da53" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360435}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fb701c86-951a-5dc2-8e1d-2b0685986ccb" :question/math-academy-id "q-37354" :question/problem "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 5 & 1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,B-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nB-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ -3 & 5 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(B-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nExpanding the determinant across the $2$nd row, we obtain the following:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ -3 & 5 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-2-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ -3 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-2-\\lambda )((1-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda )-(3)(-3)) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +2)({\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda +10) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124978 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef311af0-0e95-5574-a151-2971ad66bd08" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Eigenvalues of a 4x4 Matrix Containing a Block of Zeros"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d868ab84-6de3-56db-8f3c-ac4fdb47c961" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122891} {:answer/id #uuid "13c64a8c-b57a-5048-8c6a-78db148f5492" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122892} {:answer/id #uuid "1fb5f3ce-8662-5133-851b-929be999c756" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122893} {:answer/id #uuid "3fe66905-f33a-5d2c-b84c-24cabf303a83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122894} {:answer/id #uuid "48b715ce-7730-5b5d-bffb-669208dbf7a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122895}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "13c64a8c-b57a-5048-8c6a-78db148f5492" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122892} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab1bc0ca-1fdb-57f2-9a7b-c33a2e97dc5e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122890}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c699a77c-6393-5572-b010-6743d9f3bb17" :question/math-academy-id "q-37355" :question/problem "$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -9 & -18 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -10 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -10 & 0 \\\\ -18 & 18 & -36 & -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $P$ given above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $\\lambda =-1$ is an eigenvalue of $P$\n- $\\lambda =-10$ is an eigenvalue of $P$\n- The eigenvalue $\\lambda =-10$ has algebraic multiplicity $3$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,P-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nP-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & -9 & -18 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -10-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -10-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ -18 & 18 & -36 & -4-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(P-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nNotice that we can expand the $4\\times 4$ determinant across the $2$nd row, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & -9 & -18 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -10-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -10-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ -18 & 18 & -36 & -4-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-10-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & -18 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -10-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ -18 & -36 & -4-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, expanding the $3\\times 3$ determinant across the $2$nd row, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-10-\\lambda )\\cdot (-10-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & -3 \\\\ -18 & -4-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-10-\\lambda )^{2}((-1-\\lambda )(-4-\\lambda )-54) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +10)^{2}({\\lambda }^{2}+5\\lambda -50) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +10)^{2}(\\lambda +10)(\\lambda -5) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +10)^{3}(\\lambda -5) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the eigenvalues of $P$ are $\\lambda =-10$ (with algebraic multiplicity $3$) and $\\lambda =5.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360441 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "289ae874-f555-50ee-896f-eb2188004124" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Eigenvalues of a 3x3 Matrix Containing a Block of Zeros"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fe0382d8-ce11-556a-8bba-f884c1587f14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -8)(\\lambda +7)(\\lambda -3)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360443} {:answer/id #uuid "d959fb0f-8ecb-5c8a-b5fd-7753de4c41c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda +3)(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda +2)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360444} {:answer/id #uuid "771bf140-b753-5831-9648-6acf3648614e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda -6)(\\lambda +1)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360445} {:answer/id #uuid "b976364e-6983-545a-8c2b-af906b9adbb4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda +2)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360446} {:answer/id #uuid "5f3c6f37-9dcc-5e84-a77b-abcbb8463334" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda (\\lambda -6)(\\lambda +7)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360447}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b976364e-6983-545a-8c2b-af906b9adbb4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda +2)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360446} :answer-field/id #uuid "3661ee4a-6b05-5186-bc74-d541bbc7585a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360442}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "eddb6d20-0cb7-5e2b-9283-ce07307da093" :question/math-academy-id "q-37390" :question/problem "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}8 & 10 & 0 \\\\ -5 & -7 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -9 & 3\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,B-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nB-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}8-\\lambda  & 10 & 0 \\\\ -5 & -7-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 6 & -9 & 3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(B-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nExpanding the determinant across the $3$rd column, we obtain the following:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}8-\\lambda  & 10 & 0 \\\\ -5 & -7-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 6 & -9 & 3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}8-\\lambda  & 10 \\\\ -5 & -7-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )((8-\\lambda )(-7-\\lambda )-(-5)(10)) & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -6) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -3)(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda +2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360448 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5abea3ab-76a7-5598-8ede-b4cf88dd47d7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Eigenvalues of a General 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "614d0399-6f7f-5355-a891-c40b97a89907" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}-4{\\lambda }^{2}+49\\lambda -138=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360450} {:answer/id #uuid "21780e5a-aa2d-5246-b77f-6480f36fd2b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}-10{\\lambda }^{2}+43\\lambda -90=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360451} {:answer/id #uuid "d49cabe9-38d2-5f98-a0d0-dbc3e9cf