ed}| & =0 \\\\ (-1-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda +6)+8(-3\\lambda +9)-4(-6\\lambda +18) & =0 \\\\ (-{\\lambda }^{3}+4{\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -6)+(-24\\lambda +72)-(-24\\lambda +72) & =0 \\\\ -{\\lambda }^{3}+4{\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -6 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{3}-4{\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda +6 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360455 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5abea3ab-76a7-5598-8ede-b4cf88dd47d7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Eigenvalues of a General 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1dee7f5a-ac4e-5e24-8fed-133a1ebe71eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}-4{\\lambda }^{2}+53\\lambda +36=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360457} {:answer/id #uuid "3090eabf-d749-545f-8cd3-cf9c65d3d9c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}+4{\\lambda }^{2}-37\\lambda -72=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360458} {:answer/id #uuid "f52afe04-b5d3-594c-a6b9-66aa4eb702ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}-4{\\lambda }^{2}-37\\lambda +72=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360459} {:answer/id #uuid "8311f9f3-dc55-5bd2-a226-1642ee8ee281" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}+4{\\lambda }^{2}-37\\lambda -108=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360460} {:answer/id #uuid "c468a99f-c0b2-5c00-bccc-49e238035274" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}+4{\\lambda }^{2}-53\\lambda -36=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360461}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3090eabf-d749-545f-8cd3-cf9c65d3d9c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}+4{\\lambda }^{2}-37\\lambda -72=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360458} :answer-field/id #uuid "7dc75481-eed5-54ac-80e5-e01e14d5d5ed" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360456}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f2d4df4d-2fc7-5b45-ac94-c5220ae92532" :question/math-academy-id "q-37396" :question/problem "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}-9 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -8 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,B-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nB-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}-9-\\lambda  & 9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5-\\lambda  & -8 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(B-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nExpanding the determinant across the $1$st row, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-9-\\lambda  & 9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5-\\lambda  & -8 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-9-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}5-\\lambda  & -8 \\\\ 1 & -\\lambda \\end{aligned}|-9|\\begin{aligned}0 & -8 \\\\ -2 & -\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-9-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda +8)-9(-16) & =0 \\\\ (-{\\lambda }^{3}-4{\\lambda }^{2}+37\\lambda -72)+144 & =0 \\\\ -{\\lambda }^{3}-4{\\lambda }^{2}+37\\lambda +72 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{3}+4{\\lambda }^{2}-37\\lambda -72 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360462 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5abea3ab-76a7-5598-8ede-b4cf88dd47d7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Eigenvalues of a General 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "178742c6-30df-54a6-9afa-983ce72e4d2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in {1,-6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360464} {:answer/id #uuid "e8d1e6c9-7726-56fd-a746-66f82dff793e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in {-1,2,-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360465} {:answer/id #uuid "aeb73f3b-34ed-5b89-a489-a5e2fa5283fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in {2,-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360466} {:answer/id #uuid "1eca8a58-c362-5164-a53b-25c70af9c711" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in {-1,-2,3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360467} {:answer/id #uuid "4456285c-e35f-599b-ae8d-4471c7a3f302" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in {-1,2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360468}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1eca8a58-c362-5164-a53b-25c70af9c711" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in {-1,-2,3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360467} :answer-field/id #uuid "49f71074-aa93-5289-bc34-af112c416de2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360463}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ba3b9cc6-841d-5636-9777-0bc1e8c24e7f" :question/math-academy-id "q-80825" :question/problem "Determine all real eigenvalues $\\lambda $ of the matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is given by $det(A-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nExpanding the determinant across the $1$st row, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-1-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-{\\lambda }^{3}+6\\lambda +5)-(-1-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ -{\\lambda }^{3}+7\\lambda +6 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{3}-7\\lambda -6 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to solve this equation. We find the first root by testing some values. According to the rational zeros theorem, a list of good first guesses consists of all divisors of $6:$ \n\n$$\n\\pm 1,\\pm 2,\\pm 3,\\pm 6\n$$\n\n- Let's pick $x=1.$ Substituting to the characteristic equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(1)^{3}-7(1)-6 & =-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $\\lambda =1$ is not a root of the equation.\n\n- Let's pick $x=-1.$ Substituting to the characteristic equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1)^{3}-7(-1)-6 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $\\lambda =-1$ is a root of the equation.\n\nSo, we can factor $(\\lambda +1)$ out of ${\\lambda }^{3}-7\\lambda -6$ using synthetic division:\n\n| $-1$ | $1$ | $0$ | $-7$ | $-6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $↓$ | $-1$ | $1$ | $6$ |\n|  | $1$ | $-1$ | $-6$ | $0$ |\n\nSo, we obtain the following factorization:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda +1)({\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -6) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +1)(\\lambda +2)(\\lambda -3) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are ${\\lambda }_{1}=-1,$ $\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=-2,\\,$ and $\\,{\\lambda }_{3}=3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360469 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef311af0-0e95-5574-a151-2971ad66bd08" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Eigenvalues of a 4x4 Matrix Containing a Block of Zeros"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "99ef1261-29d5-5c12-9eaa-dc191cc40c44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -3)^{2}(\\lambda -2)(\\lambda -1)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360471} {:answer/id #uuid "767f2c83-ff07-595e-ac4a-c24f9382a823" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda +{3}^{2})(\\lambda +2)(\\lambda -1)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360472} {:answer/id #uuid "5a82c8eb-7cb4-5e10-896c-527d136aa2eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda -2)(\\lambda -1)(\\lambda +3)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360473} {:answer/id #uuid "d77d3a94-0fde-5916-851f-e9e6603ba1db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -3)^{2}(\\lambda +2)(\\lambda -1)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360474} {:answer/id #uuid "31845830-b226-5f9e-9b64-703e12a8d734" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda +2)(\\lambda -1)(\\lambda +3)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360475}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "31845830-b226-5f9e-9b64-703e12a8d734" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda +2)(\\lambda -1)(\\lambda +3)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360475} :answer-field/id #uuid "dfee94dc-1ded-5fec-a74a-56f360247b0c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360470}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5abaedb5-7997-51fd-b21a-260cfe3dbc5e" :question/math-academy-id "q-86749" :question/problem "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n$P=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,P-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nP-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & 5 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2-\\lambda  & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1-\\lambda  & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(P-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nSince the determinant of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix is given by the product of the entries on the main diagonal, we obtain the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & 5 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2-\\lambda  & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1-\\lambda  & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )(-2-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda )(-3-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -3)(\\lambda +2)(\\lambda -1)(\\lambda +3) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360476 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5abea3ab-76a7-5598-8ede-b4cf88dd47d7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Eigenvalues of a General 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ea45ba8-3eac-5207-8bc7-2d0e02c70b64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in {-2,-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360478} {:answer/id #uuid "c0046a85-aaf9-5ddc-86d6-624075345a6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in {-2,1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360479} {:answer/id #uuid "d38ebc87-e8af-57d0-a9aa-f88cd14aaffb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in {-1,1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360480} {:answer/id #uuid "f687f430-e93a-572e-ae24-706a454b6eb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in {-2,-1,1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360481} {:answer/id #uuid "a6e22436-50f0-5d3c-8827-b21fe19d0a39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in {2,-1,1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360482}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f687f430-e93a-572e-ae24-706a454b6eb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in {-2,-1,1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360481} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4e47216-2ae5-5fec-ba60-2fa2e1a1d6fc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360477}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8b75d1ac-303a-511c-86a2-e86c1eaa7201" :question/math-academy-id "q-86758" :question/problem "Determine all real eigenvalues $\\lambda $ of the matrix \n$O=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,O-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nO-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is given by $det(O-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nExpanding the determinant across the $1$st row, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(O-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-1-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ 1 & -\\lambda \\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1-\\lambda  \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-{\\lambda }^{3}-2{\\lambda }^{2}+1)+(\\lambda +1) & =0 \\\\ -{\\lambda }^{3}-2{\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda +2 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{3}+2{\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -2 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to solve this equation. We find the first root by testing some values. According to the rational zeros theorem, a list of good first guesses consists of all divisors of $2:$ \n\n$$\n\\pm 1,\\pm 2\n$$\n\nLet's pick $x=1.$ Substituting to the characteristic equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(1)^{3}+2(1)^{2}-(1)-2 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $\\lambda =1$ is a root of the equation. So, we can factor $(\\lambda -1)$ out of ${\\lambda }^{3}+2{\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -2$ using synthetic division:\n\n| $1$ | $1$ | $2$ | $-1$ | $-2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $↓$ | $1$ | $3$ | $2$ |\n|  | $1$ | $3$ | $2$ | $0$ |\n\nSo, we obtain the following factorization:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda -1)({\\lambda }^{2}+3\\lambda +2) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -1)(\\lambda +2)(\\lambda +1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are ${\\lambda }_{1}=1,$ $\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=-2,\\,$ and $\\,{\\lambda }_{3}=-1.$"}]}
